  "common_review": {
    "dos": "Both have the same conventional 64-byte MZ header and 14-byte DOS code stub: push cs; pop ds; mov dx,14; mov ah,9; int 21h; mov ax,0x4c01; int 21h. This prints the embedded fixed DOS incompatibility message and exits with code one under DOS. It is not the Windows entry point.",
    "rich": "The pre-PE bytes contain the conventional Microsoft Rich build metadata and zero padding; not mapped as executable code.",
    "capabilities": "Windows code has no imports, dynamic loading, filesystem, network, credential access, processes or persistence. The export returns a pointer to fixed data; DllMain returns TRUE. The x64 entry saves its three arguments in caller-provided home slots. No TLS callbacks, load-config callbacks, resource scripts, exception handlers or delay-imports.",
    "permissions": "Code is read/execute; data read/write; read-only metadata is non-executable. No writable executable section."
  },
